{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119528","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119528/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119528/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119528/events","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/119528","id":4465082884,"node_id":"I_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABCiPCBA","number":119528,"title":"Sprite2D loses pixels at integer positions in small/pixel games with integer scaling","user":{"login":"scrybil","id":158219161,"node_id":"U_kgDOCW47mQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/158219161?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/scrybil","html_url":"https://github.com/scrybil","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scrybil/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scrybil/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scrybil/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scrybil/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scrybil/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scrybil/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scrybil/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scrybil/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scrybil/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":279096997,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTY5OTc=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/archived","name":"archived","color":"aaaaaa","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":2,"created_at":"2026-05-17T22:07:36Z","updated_at":"2026-05-18T08:18:43Z","closed_at":"2026-05-18T01:28:31Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Originally found in Godot 4.6.2\n- Reproduceable until 4.7 beta 2\n- Reproduceable in 4.0\n\n### System information\n\nWindows 11 - Godot 4.6.2 stable - Compatibility - AMD Radeon(TM) Graphics (Ryzen 5 7535U)\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen moving a player character around in a small scene (particularly 640x360), pixels will shift or disappear if the player character is at a perfect integer position. I would imagine that pixels are not meant to disappear at those positions.\n\nAt an integer position:\n<img width=\"1920\" height=\"1140\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/ac9846f0-8f70-4912-b874-7fb0804b3a61\" />\n\nAt a floating point position:\n\n<img width=\"1920\" height=\"1140\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/8141a684-278c-4f49-a5e3-3abb133bfa40\" />\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nUsing the MRP, open it and run the program, move the character around with your arrow keys and observe the pixels disappearing. You can toggle snapping to integer positions using the button to the right of the screen.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[pixel_disappearing_bug.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/27928661/pixel_disappearing_bug.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"scrybil","id":158219161,"node_id":"U_kgDOCW47mQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/158219161?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/scrybil","html_url":"https://github.com/scrybil","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scrybil/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scrybil/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scrybil/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/use